artifacts/*
!artifacts/.gitkeep
!artifacts/**/.gitkeep
# The round-1 worklist is derived from public CVE data and from the
# driver's own release tags, so it is the same kind of committed data as
# tools/ioctl_map.json. Round 1 reads it before any campaign has run, and
# regenerating it needs network access to the PSIRT bulletins and a
# tagged checkout, so a fresh clone that lacked it would start blind.
!artifacts/surface/
artifacts/surface/*
!artifacts/surface/worklist-round1.md
# The Track U harnesses are hand-written C and Go, and no phase
# regenerates them: they were authored offline from the container
# sources at a pinned commit. Losing them to a clone would lose the
# work outright. Their seed corpora and dictionaries are inputs and
# belong with them. Campaign output goes to artifacts/runs/ and stays
# ignored.
!artifacts/harnesses/
!artifacts/harnesses/**
state/*
!state/.gitkeep
# knowledge/ itself is committed on purpose — it is the only thing that
# survives a rebuilt box. Its lock files are not.
knowledge/*.lock
__pycache__/
*.pyc
thoughts/
tmp/
.claude/settings.local.json
# The documentation site's build output and toolchain. package.json and
# package-lock.json are committed; CI installs from the lockfile.
docs/node_modules/
docs/dist/
docs/.astro/
